  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "The only pattern whose mechanism directly matches this workflow is P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE, since the workflow already defines concurrency group docker-apply-cache with cancel-in-progress: false. However, the workflow publishes a renv dependency image to GHCR (packages: write, docker login/push in update-renv-cache and prune-dependency-images), which is release/deployment work, an explicit contraindication of P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE; the shared concurrency group also spans manual dispatches and PR merges, raising the distinct-branches cancellation risk. No other pattern's preconditions are verifiably satisfied: there is no Bazel build (P-LIT-BAZEL-*), the CI history is marked not_a_measured_baseline/historical_context_only so no safe timeout can be derived (P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT/P-LIT-HISTORY-TIMEOUT), required checks are unverified and the repository path structure is unknown (P-LIT-CHANGE-FILTER and change-based selection), and the workflow already avoids redundant image builds via its image-exists check. Applying a change risks cancelling publishing work or omitting required coverage, so no supported optimization is applied.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE"]
}
